# Rust — the Cargo workspace target dir lives at the repo root
/target

# ── Secrets — NEVER publish ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The update-signing private key lives in ~/.tauri, outside this tree. These
# patterns are a backstop in case a key is ever copied in here by accident.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*password*.txt
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Internal planning documents — NEVER publish ───────────────────────────
# The repo is public (source-available). Product strategy, the PLAID planning
# artifacts and the proprietary style research stay in the working tree only.
# Public docs added by later tasks (docs/legal/, docs/runbooks/, docs/daw-matrix.md)
# are deliberately NOT covered by these paths and remain tracked.
/vision.json
/scripts/validate-vision.js
/docs/gtm.md
/docs/prd.md
/docs/product-roadmap.md
/docs/product-vision.md
# ⛔ A GLOB, not the single filename it used to be. The compendium grew a
# five-volume companion set (`style-research-extended.md`,
# `-extended-2.md` … `-extended-underground.md`) and the exact-path rule above
# covered none of them — they sat untracked but NOT ignored, one `git add -A`
# away from being published. This is the dataset's whole moat: the research is
# what nobody else has, and `docs/` is what the Pages site publishes from, so a
# stray commit here is a publication.
/docs/style-research*.md

# House-convention planning files (same names as the sibling Freally repos)
